Package: ananicy-cpp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, cachyos-ananicy-rules, sparky-stereo-problems
Description: Auto nice daemon, a C++ rewrite of Ananicy
 Sets the nice value, scheduling class, I/O class, OOM score, CPU affinity
 and cgroup of running programs from rule files. The unit is enabled and
 started on installation, as CachyOS ships it; a person's own choice (systemctl
 disable) is kept across upgrades. A start the kernel does not allow (no BTF,
 BPF refused) is told through the shared problems engine and is not repeated.
 The package ships no rules.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Paweł "pavroo"
 Pijanowski). Upstream: Vladislav Nepogodin and the ananicy-cpp contributors;
 the idea and the first rules are Nefelim4ag's Ananicy.
